    "lawCode": "Amd §§213 & 218, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "State Finance Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A2819\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act to amend the state finance law, in relation to including eligible\nbusinesses located in certain areas designated pursuant to the federal\nCommunity Renewal Tax Relief Act of 2000 in the state's Excelsior Linked\nDeposit Act loan program\n\nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\nThis bill will allow qualifying businesses located in certain areas\ndesignated under the Federal Community Renewal Tax Relief Act of 2000 to\nbe eligible for numerous loans at the most beneficial interest rate\nprovided through the Excelsior Linked Deposit program.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n§ 1 - Amends § 213 of the State Finance Law by adding four new subdivi-\nsions 12-a, 12-b, 22 and 23 to define \"empowerment zone\", \"enterprise\ncommunity\", \"renewal community\" and \"renewal community business.\"\n\n§ 2 - Amends subdivision 11 of §2l3 of the State Finance Law by adding\nthree new paragraphs (b-1), (b-2) and (b-3) that include a business\nlocated in a renewal community, empowerment zone or enterprise community\nwithin the definition of an eligible business.\n\n§ 3 - Amends paragraph (c) of subdivision 12 of §213 of the State\nFinance Law to add eligible businesses that are located in a renewal\ncommunity, empowerment zone or enterprise community within the defi-\nnition of eligible projects.\n\n§ 4 - Amends paragraph (a) of subdivision 16 of §213 of the State\nFinance Law to add eligible businesses that are located in a renewal\ncommunity, empowerment zone or enterprise community within the defi-\nnition of linked deposit interest rate.\n\n§ 5 - Amends subdivision 1 of § 218 of the State Finance Law to add\neligible businesses that are located in a renewal community, empowerment\nzone or enterprise community to provisions regarding interest rates for\nlinked loans and the lenders fees.\n\n§ 6 - Effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThe Linked Deposit Program leverages loans from participating banks and\nother lending institutions at a reduced interest rate. In exchange, the\nstate accepts a commensurately lower return on short-term deposits\nplaced with the lenders that are used for the linked loans.\n\nCurrently, small businesses located in Empire Zones or in highly\ndistressed areas, and minority-owned and women-owned businesses or\ndefense industry manufacturers seeking financing for specified eligible\nprojects, are eligible for a linked loan interest rate three percentage\npoints below the interest rate the lender would charge absent the linked\n\ndeposit. This measure would include businesses located in federal empow-\nerment zones, enterprise communities and renewal communities within this\ncategory. All other linked loans are two percentage points below the\nrate the lender would otherwise charge.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n2007-2008: A.3265/S.4784\n2005-2006: A.3209/S.445\n2003-2004: A.6477/S.3432\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nYet to be determined.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
